    {
      "id": "0t4hy7w",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Code of Criminal Procedure (CrPC) – Now Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita (BNSS) 2023"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The BNSS replaced the CrPC effective from July 1, 2024. Important provisions for SI exam:",
      "id": "2te0734"
    },
    {
      "id": "n9jqt56",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "First Information Report (FIR) - Under Section 173 BNSS (old Section 154 CrPC), police must register FIR for cognizable offences",
        "Arrest without warrant - Cognizable offences allow arrest without warrant by police",
        "Remand - Accused can be sent to police custody for up to 15 days by Magistrate",
        "Bail - Non-bailable offences require court permission; bailable offences can be granted bail by police",
        "Charge Sheet - Police must file charge sheet within 60 days (90 days for serious offences) or accused gets default bail",
        "Section 41 BNSS (old Sec 41 CrPC) - When police can arrest without warrant"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ya3mkll",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Madhya Pradesh-Specific Acts and Laws"
    },
    {
      "id": "y1uh6ll",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "MP Police Act, 1961 - Governs organization and functioning of MP Police",
        "MP Goondas Act, 1936 - Preventive detention of habitual offenders",
        "MP Atrocities Act provisions - SC/ST Protection of Civil Rights Act enforcement",
        "MP Prohibition Act - Related to liquor prohibition enforcement",
        "MP Land Revenue Code, 1959 - Revenue laws for land records",
        "MP Panchayat Raj Act, 1993 - Local governance laws"
      ]
    },
